.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s68\",\"d1\",5043,5404,\"Both PIs are basic and/or translational researchers\\nBoth PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s69\",\"d1\",5404,5672,\"Note: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s70\",\"d1\",5672,5924,\"Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s71\",\"d1\",5924,6311,\"Extending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. ​You can see a full list of these countries on our page about extending the reach of EHA Grants.\\nIf you have questions about your eligibility, you can contact us at [email protected] before submitting an application.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s72\",\"d1\",6311,6631,\"What an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant covers\\nTo reflect the collaborative spirit of the grant, the budget must be divided 50:50 between the two PIs. If this is not the case, a justification must be provided. In any case, no more than 70% of the total grant should be allocated to one PI.\\nYou can use your grant for:\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s73\",\"d1\",6631,6988,\"Personnel costs, including the applicant or the costs of hiring other research staff to wo