th PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\nNote: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nTopics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection proce\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4026, \"end\": 4045, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 19}, {\"start\": 4100, \"end\": 4159, \"excerpt_start\": 20, \"excerpt_end\": 79}, {\"start\": 4536, \"end\": 6058, \"excerpt_start\": 80, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Research Grants\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · June 16, 2026\\nJune 16, 2026\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Research Grants are designed to support the future of hematology by helping talented junior researchers to:\\nConduct basic or translational lab-based research\\nGain valuable research and leadership experience\\nMove towards becoming group leaders\\nAdvance their careers\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nTypes of EHA Research Grants\\nThe three types of EHA Research Grant are the:\\nEHA Junior Research Grant, which can provide up to €150,000 for three years\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years\\nEach one of the three types of EHA Research Grant also has its own specific eligibility criteria. Please make sure you read the eligibility criteria for your grant type before you apply.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the sele\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"title\": \"Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 3974, \"end\": 5007, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1033}, {\"start\": 5248, \"end\": 5268, \"excerpt_start\": 1034, \"excerpt_end\": 1054}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Grants\\nEHA’s foundations are built upon our belief that it’s the collective endeavors of our community—in research and clinical practice—that lead to exponential advancements.\\nWe’re committed to accelerating progress in hematology by promoting collaboration, education, and research across all levels.\\nAn important way of achieving this is through the careful and selective allocation of grants and funding to aspiring scientists and researchers.\\nTo check which of our grants you can apply for, use the filters below. Alternatively, you can read about our different grant categories:\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nIn this section, you can also learn about EHA Travel Grants, funding from non-EHA sources and browse our grant-winners hall of fame.\\nEHA Advanced Research Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Junior Research Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Physician Scientist Research Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\"], \"visited_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants\", \"title\": \"Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/about-our-eha-research-grants\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation/grants/eha-bilateral-collaborative-grant\", \"title\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\"}], \"visited_doc_count\": 4, \"omitted_visited_d