\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants support collaboration between two independent research groups with complementarity of expertise and showing a mutual need to answer a specific research question.\\nSuccessful applicants can receive up to €320,000 for two years to be divided equally between the two research groups .\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nBoth principal investigators (PIs) are EHA members\\nBoth PIs are basic and/or translational researchers\\nBoth PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\nNote: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nTopics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection proce\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4026, \"end\": 4045, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 19}, {\"start\": 4100, \"end\": 4159, \"excerpt